<title>PORTUGAL: World refined copper consumption up mth/mth Oct 96.</title>
<headline>World refined copper consumption up mth/mth Oct 96.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Global refined copper consumption and mine and refined production of copper rose month-on-month in October 1996 and overall the market appeared to be roughly in balance, the International Copper Study Group (ICSG) said.</p>
<p>The ICSG said in a statement that consumption was only marginally lower than the rate of production for October.</p>
<p>Supply/demand calculations indicated an estimated surplus of about 65,000 tonnes for the first 10 months of 1996, it said.</p>
